<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">03032026</say-as>.</s> <s>The fourteenth of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="rɑmɑˈdɑːn">Ramadan</phoneme>, fourteen forty-seven.</s> <s>It's morning in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>, just after <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="fædʒɚ">Fajr</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>United States Marines shot dead ten people outside the American consulate in Karachi as protesters stormed the compound, demonstrating against Washington's strikes on Iran.</s> <s>Pakistan, home to the world's second-largest Shia population, has not condemned the killings — a silence explained by its deep financial dependency on Washington, even as its streets are in open revolt.</s> <s>Shia leaders have called for further protests in Lahore and Karachi despite a nationwide government ban on public gatherings, leaving a nuclear-armed state teetering on the edge of a domestic crisis.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In conflict and security.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Russia struck a Ukrainian passenger train overnight, killing eight people — part of a February that logged two hundred and eighty-eight overnight missile strikes, more than double January's count and the highest monthly total in three years.</s> <s>The surge unfolded while global attention was fixed on the Iran war, a window Moscow appears to have deliberately exploited.</s> <s>Ukraine's railways chief warned the strikes are designed to sever entire regions from the national network.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In South Sudan, armed youth from Unity state killed one hundred and sixty-nine people in the oil-rich <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ruˈwɛŋ">Ruweng</phoneme> area, attacking the predominantly Dinka community there.</s> <s>The massacre followed the arrest of opposition leader Riek <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmɑtʃɑr">Machar</phoneme>, effectively ending the country's fragile 2018 peace agreement.</s> <s>Doctors Without Borders has suspended all medical services in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="dʒɔŋˈleɪ">Jonglei</phoneme> state, leaving a vast region without emergency care.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israeli authorities sealed the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="æl ˈæk.sɑ">Al-Aqsa</phoneme> mosque compound for a third consecutive day — the first Ramadan closure since Israel occupied East Jerusalem in 1967.</s> <s>Hundreds of thousands of worshippers are being denied access to the third holiest site in Islam during the holiest month of the year.</s> <s>Over one thousand Jerusalem residents have been individually banned from the compound, with no timeline for reopening.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Spain stands alone among North Atlantic Treaty Organization members in refusing Washington's request to use its military bases for strikes on Iran, with Prime Minister Pedro <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈsɑntʃɛz">Sánchez</phoneme> calling the campaign unjustified.</s> <s>Britain reversed course over the weekend, authorizing American access and splitting the alliance between those treating the war as collective defence and those unwilling to be drawn in.</s> <s>It is the sharpest public rupture NATO has seen since the Iraq war debates of 2003.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Lebanon's Prime Minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="nɑˈwɑf sɑˈlɑm">Nawaf Salam</phoneme> ordered <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌhɛz.bəˈlɑː">Hezbollah</phoneme> to disarm after Israel killed thirty-one people in Beirut, following rocket fire from Lebanese territory.</s> <s>It is an extraordinary demand from a government that has long coexisted with the armed group, and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌhɛz.bəˈlɑː">Hezbollah</phoneme> has not publicly responded.</s> <s>Salam has asked the United States and France to press Israel for a ceasefire — a request directed at two capitals currently committed to the war.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>France has offered to station nuclear-armed aircraft in allied nations, with President Emmanuel Macron declaring that American distraction in Iran has proved Europe can no longer outsource its own security.</s> <s>Macron said that to be free, a nation must be feared.</s> <s>Allied governments now face a decision no European capital has confronted since the Cold War — whether to accept French nuclear cover, and what sovereignty they trade for it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Argentina's Senate voted forty-four to twenty-seven to make fourteen-year-olds criminally liable, replacing a juvenile justice code that has stood since 1980.</s> <s>President Javier <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="miˈleɪ">Milei</phoneme> will sign the bill within days — his second major legislation this week, following a labour reform already challenged in court by trade unions.</s> <s>Critics warn that Argentina's detention centres lack the capacity to hold the newly eligible prisoners.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Seven hundred and fifty vessels are stranded outside the Strait of Hormuz after Iran's Revolutionary Guard declared it will fire on any ship attempting passage.</s> <s>The strait carries twenty-one percent of the world's daily oil supply, and its closure has driven crude prices sharply higher while disrupting liquefied natural gas flows that Europe and Asia depend on.</s> <s>India and Japan hold roughly ninety days of strategic petroleum reserves — their only buffer if the blockade holds.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Washington has removed Vietnam from its export control list, lifting restrictions that had placed Hanoi in the same category as Beijing, Moscow, and Pyongyang, blocking access to advanced chip-manufacturing equipment.</s> <s>Vietnam's state telecom, <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="viˈɛt.tɛl">Viettel</phoneme>, is now targeting trial chip production by late 2027.</s> <s>The decision signals Washington's intent to build Southeast Asia into a genuine manufacturing alternative to China in the global semiconductor supply chain.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India and Canada signed a two-point-six billion dollar uranium deal, with Prime Minister Mark Carney flying to Delhi for the ceremony.</s> <s>The agreement ends a three-year diplomatic freeze that began when Ottawa accused the Indian government of ordering the assassination of a Sikh activist on Canadian soil.</s> <s>Deliveries begin in 2027, making the relationship transactional again — whether it can become genuinely warm is another matter.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Researchers at Columbia University have redesigned immune cells to detect cancer at signal levels fifty times fainter than existing therapies can register, directly targeting the mechanism that lets solid tumours hide from the immune system.</s> <s>In laboratory tests where conventional immunotherapy failed entirely, the new receptor succeeded.</s> <s>A Phase One clinical trial targeting ovarian cancer is now in planning, with the approach potentially applicable to many tumour types that currently have no effective treatment.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A Swedish investigation has found that workers at a contractor in Nairobi annotate video footage from seven million Ray-Ban smart glasses to train Meta's artificial intelligence — footage that includes intimate scenes inside people's homes, their conversations, and the faces of their children.</s> <s>Meta is developing facial recognition for the same glasses, triggering regulatory inquiries from Italy and Ireland.</s> <s>The findings expose the human surveillance infrastructure behind what the company markets as an artificial intelligence feature.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Two Kremlin sources say Russia will block Telegram in April, cutting off the platform's ninety million Russian users from the country's last major channel for independent news and anti-war organizing.</s> <s>The move follows Telegram founder Pavel Durov's arrest in France last year and his subsequent cooperation with European authorities, which gave Moscow a pretext it had long been waiting for.</s> <s>No confirmed alternative platform remains freely accessible from inside Russia.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
<break time="500ms"/>
<s>We'll be back this evening in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>, around <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="mɑːɡɹɪb">Maghrib</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="300ms"/>
<s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔɪn ʃæːʔ ɑɫ.ɫɑːh">إن شاء الله</phoneme>.</s>
</speak>